Not necessary. But JSON string inside the \"implementation\" value does not need to escape single quotes. So it's okay.\n\nBut we should also ensure that the returned object from solve(case) is JSON-serializable. Our dict is fine.\n\nLet's test mentally against fixtures.\n\nCase 0: attempts non-empty, last success=> stop, current_num=1, next_attempt=1, memory_append with reflection \"adjust-0\", signature \"e0\". Good.\n\nCase 1: three failures, no repeat, budget not exhausted => continue, next_attempt=4, memory_append last reflection \"adjust-2\", signature \"e2\". Good.\n\nCase 2: four failures, last failure signature e0 repeated (first also e0) => stop, current_num=4, next_attempt=4, memory_append last reflection \"adjust-3\", signature \"e0\". Good.\n\nEdge: empty attempts: continue next_attempt=1 memory_append null.\n\nAll good.\n\nNow produce final JSON. Ensure no trailing spaces, just the object."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1265,"completion_tokens":3727,"total_tokens":4992,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1152},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3383},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1152,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":113},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}